# Secrets and live state. `data/` holds the SQLite database, the app secret
# key (CSRF tokens derive from it) and the operator API bearer token --
# anyone holding that token has full operator access over the network,
# including unsafe SQL writes and credential resets. None of it belongs in
# version control.
data/
certs/
backup_data/
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Operator GUI exports. The Billing and Tables tabs write CSVs to whatever
# directory they are pointed at, which in practice is often the project
# root -- billing-account-2.csv was sitting here. These contain real
# account, worker and billing data.
*.csv

# Internal engineering record: unfinished work, scale limits, open
# questions. Kept out of version control deliberately rather than merely
# out of the README, because git history is permanent -- a file committed
# once stays readable in every clone even after a later commit deletes it.
# Back this up separately; it is not in the repo.
docs/ENGINEERING_NOTES.md

.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
node_modules/
.claude/

# Review documents (not part of the project)
autorack-verify-architecture-recommendations*.pdf
autorack-verify-code-review*.pdf
